{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions can contain Octane nodes or renderer components for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":". Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so function components become Octane element descriptors with the correct typed context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the recommended TSRX component. Give it exactly one table object: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<table.FlexRender header={header} />\n<table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n<table.FlexRender footer={header} />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The table instance exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":", and the component can also be imported directly from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/octane-table"},{"type":"text","value":". Rendering it as a component gives Octane the correct component scope while preserving strings, numbers (including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":"), and pre-created descriptors."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" when appropriate, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and suppresses grouping placeholder cells."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRender } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane function components are converted with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createElement"},{"type":"text","value":"; non-function nodes pass through unchanged. Unlike React, Octane has no class-component, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardRef"},{"type":"text","value":", or exotic-component branch. The lower-level function also does not select grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" in normal TSRX table markup. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" before rendering a header unless a spanning layout intentionally uses the placeholder, and pass footer-group "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Header"},{"type":"text","value":" objects through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" prop."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nColumn definitions can contain Octane nodes or renderer components for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so function components become Octane element descriptors with the correct typed context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended TSRX component. Give it exactly one table object: `cell`, `header`, or `footer`.\n\n```tsx\n<table.FlexRender header={header} />\n<table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n<table.FlexRender footer={header} />\n```\n\nThe table instance exposes `FlexRender`, and the component can also be imported directly from `@tanstack/octane-table`. Rendering it as a component gives Octane the correct component scope while preserving strings, numbers (including `0`), and pre-created descriptors.\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` when appropriate, falls back to `cell`, and suppresses grouping placeholder cells.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:\n\n```tsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nOctane function components are converted with `createElement`; non-function nodes pass through unchanged. Unlike React, Octane has no class-component, `forwardRef`, or exotic-component branch. The lower-level function also does not select grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders.\n\nUse `FlexRender` in normal TSRX table markup. Check `header.isPlaceholder` before rendering a header unless a spanning layout intentionally uses the placeholder, and pass footer-group `Header` objects through the `footer` prop.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Octane) Guide\n---\n\nColumn definitions can contain Octane nodes or renderer components for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so function components become Octane element descriptors with the correct typed context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended TSRX component. Give it exactly one table object: `cell`, `header`, or `footer`.\n\n```tsx\n<table.FlexRender header={header} />\n<table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n<table.FlexRender footer={header} />\n```\n\nThe table instance exposes `FlexRender`, and the component can also be imported directly from `@tanstack/octane-table`. Rendering it as a component gives Octane the correct component scope while preserving strings, numbers (including `0`), and pre-created descriptors.\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` when appropriate, falls back to `cell`, and suppresses grouping placeholder cells.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:\n\n```tsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nOctane function components are converted with `createElement`; non-function nodes pass through unchanged. Unlike React, Octane has no class-component, `forwardRef`, or exotic-component branch. The lower-level function also does not select grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders.\n\nUse `FlexRender` in normal TSRX table markup. Check `header.isPlaceholder` before rendering a header unless a spanning layout intentionally uses the placeholder, and pass footer-group `Header` objects through the `footer` prop.\n"}
